\cf2 Alexander continued his commentary. \'93Now here the leader of the group starts playing an excessively gratuitous solo which, according to heavy metallurgists, is a key part of the mind entrainment.\'94 He allowed that to play on a little. \'93Now watch carefully. And a warning: what you\'92re about to see will be extremely distressing. Yes, these are our own Airborne children being hemmed in by the crowd.  What you\'92re about to see, according to expert gerontologists, is the moment our captive children are possessed by demons. There it is!\'94\
On the screen, the kids were playing air guitars.\
The more exuberant ones were playing them behind their heads.\
Alexander admired the splicing; the edit made the transition from the Sages on stage to the kids in the audience seamless.\
Then the images cut to kids throwing up Elvi cocktails in the Botanic Gardens.\
\'93Shocking,\'94 Alexander said with fake gravitas. The footage showed more kids playing air guitars.\
\'93Now watch as the camera pans,\'94 Alexander guided.\
The image went white again while the camera adjusted to the stage lighting. After a second the Sages could be seen still performing on the stage. Then the camera slowly panned around until the production tower could be seen in the distance. The camera zoomed; beneath the tower a platform resolved from the blur. People seemed to be seated up there, two on thrones. The image froze.\
\'93Now, if we zoom in, who do we find sitting up there among the demonic royalty?\'94\
The image zoomed in. It was grainy, but damning. Eloise was there, presiding over the frenzy.\
Back live in the Lysander, Alexander turned to the captive Eloise. \'93You really do like that office chair, don\'92t you, mother?\'94\
